{"text":"That to be good wife material, she has to be, to use that Nigerian word, very homely. And then she got married, and after a while her husband's family began to complain that she had changed. Actually, she had not changed, she just got tired of pretending. The problem, the problem with gender, is that it prescribes how we should be, rather than recognizing how we are. Now imagine how much happier we would be, how much freer to be our true individual selves if we didn't have the weight of gender expectations. Boys and girls are undeniably different biologically, but socialization exaggerates the differences, and then it becomes a self-fulfilling process. Now take cooking, for example. Today women in general are more likely to do the house walk than men, the cooking and cleaning. But why is that?","words":[{"text":"That","start":0.0,"end":0.38},{"text":"to","start":0.38,"end":0.58},{"text":"be","start":0.58,"end":0.88},{"text":"good","start":0.88,"end":1.44},{"text":"wife","start":1.44,"end":1.8},{"text":"material","start":1.8,"end":2.44,"punct":","},{"text":"she","start":2.88,"end":2.9},{"text":"has","start":2.9,"end":3.06},{"text":"to","start":3.06,"end":3.3},{"text":"be","start":3.3,"end":3.56,"punct":","},{"text":"to","start":3.58,"end":3.86},{"text":"use","start":3.86,"end":4.0},{"text":"that","start":4.0,"end":4.18},{"text":"Nigerian","start":4.18,"end":4.5},{"text":"word","start":4.5,"end":4.86,"punct":","},{"text":"very","start":5.14,"end":5.46},{"text":"homely","start":5.46,"end":6.54,"punct":"."},{"text":"And","start":7.9,"end":8.02},{"text":"then","start":8.02,"end":8.14},{"text":"she","start":8.14,"end":8.28},{"text":"got","start":8.28,"end":8.44},{"text":"married","start":8.44,"end":8.82,"punct":","},{"text":"and","start":9.44,"end":9.52},{"text":"after","start":9.52,"end":9.68},{"text":"a","start":9.68,"end":9.84},{"text":"while","start":9.84,"end":9.96},{"text":"her","start":9.96,"end":10.12},{"text":"husband's","start":10.12,"end":10.56},{"text